- Looking an element up by number gives an [optional](optional-values.md) value, since a
- number may have no element.
+ Das Nachschlagen eines Elements über die Zahl liefert einen [optionalen](optional-values.md)
+ Wert, da zu einer Zahl kein Element gehören kann.

- ### Molecules
+ ### Moleküle

- Atoms are bonded into a molecule with `*`, and an atom which is repeated takes its number as
- a type argument. A molecule is written out with proper subscripts:
+ Atome werden mit `*` zu einem Molekül verbunden, und ein wiederholtes Atom nimmt seine Anzahl
+ als Typargument. Ein Molekül wird mit korrekten tiefgestellten Zeichen ausgeschrieben:

= a type argument. A molecule is written out with proper subscripts:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val water = H[2]*O
+ val water = H[2]*O

= val water = H[2]*O
- ```
+ ```

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val water = H[2]*O
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(water.show)
+ Out.println(water.show)

- Out.println((C*O[2]).show)
+ Out.println((C*O[2]).show)

- Out.println((C[6]*H[12]*O[6]).show)
+ Out.println((C[6]*H[12]*O[6]).show)

= Out.println((C[6]*H[12]*O[6]).show)
- ```
+ ```

- ### Formulas and equations
+ ### Formeln und Gleichungen

- A molecule with a coefficient is a term of a formula. Terms are added with `+`, and two
- formulas are joined into an equation with a reaction arrow:
+ Ein Molekül mit einem Koeffizienten ist ein Term einer Formel. Terme werden mit `+` addiert,
+ und zwei Formeln werden mit einem Reaktionspfeil zu einer Gleichung verbunden:

= formulas are joined into an equation with a reaction arrow:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2
+ val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2

= val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2
- ```
+ ```

= val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2
= ```
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= val combustion = H[2]*2 + O[2] --> H[2]*O*2
= ```
=
= ```scala fuel
= run
- ##
+ ##

- Out.println(combustion.show)
+ Out.println(combustion.show)

= Out.println(combustion.show)
- ```
+ ```

- An equation knows whether its two sides contain the same atoms:
+ Eine Gleichung weiß, ob ihre beiden Seiten dieselben Atome enthalten:

= An equation knows whether its two sides contain the same atoms:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= An equation knows whether its two sides contain the same atoms:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
+ run

= An equation knows whether its two sides contain the same atoms:
